\n- All entities implement tenant isolation via FK to `Tenant` table\n- Composite keys for join tables ensure multi-tenant data separation\n- Optimistic locking via `@Version` column\n- `@PrePersist`/`@PreUpdate` hooks for timestamp management\n- JSON columns for flexible metadata (categories, collections, SEO, custom attributes, option values)\n\n#### 2. Repositories (Data Access Layer)\n\nAll repositories implement `PanacheRepositoryBase` with tenant-scoped queries:\n- `/Users/tea/dev/VillageCompute/code/village-storefront/modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/data/repositories/ProductRepository.java` - 268 lines with 16 query methods including:\n  - `findByCurrentTenant()`, `findActiveByCurrentTenant()`, `findByStatusForCurrentTenant()`\n  - `findBySku()`, `findBySlug()`, `findByIdAndTenant()`\n  - `searchProducts()`, `searchProductsByNameOrSku()`\n  - `findActiveByCategorySlug()`, `findActiveByCollectionSlug()`, `findActiveByCategoryAndCollection()` with pagination support\n  \n- `ProductVariantRepository.java` - 73 lines with tenant-scoped queries:\n  - `findByProduct()`, `findBySku()`, `findByIdForTenant()`\n  \n- `CategoryRepository.java` - 95 lines with hierarchical queries:\n  - `findByCurrentTenant()`, `findByCode()`, `findBySlug()`\n  - `findRootCategories()`, `findByParent()` for hierarchy navigation\n  \n- `CollectionRepository.java` - 158 lines with 11 query methods:\n  - `findByCurrentTenant()`, `findByStatus()`, `findByCode()`, `findBySlug()`\n  - `findPublished()`, `searchCollections()`, `countByStatus()`, `countByCurrentTenant()`\n\n#### 3. Services (Business Logic)\n\n- `/Users/tea/dev/VillageCompute/code/village-storefront/modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/services/CatalogService.java` - 705 lines covering:\n  - **Product Operations:** create, update, get, list with filtering, search, count, delete (soft)\n  - **Category Operations:** create, update, getRootCategories, getChildCategories, delete\n  - **Collection Operations:** create, update, get, getBySlug, listPublished, listByStatus, delete\n  - **Variant Operations:** create, getProductVariants, getVariantBySku\n  - OpenTelemetry span instrumentation and metrics recording\n  - Cache invalidation hooks via `CatalogCacheService`\n  - Full validation pipeline via `CatalogValidator`\n  - `CatalogSearchResult` record for pagination\n\n- `CatalogJobService.java` - 224 lines for async import/export operations:\n  - Priority-based job queue management\n  - Job scheduling with retry policies\n  - Enqueue operations for import/export jobs\n  - Queue depth monitoring\n  - Feature flag enforcement\n\n- `CatalogCacheService.java` - Caffeine-based caching for search results:\n  - Tenant-isolated cache keys (tenantId + query hash)\n  - Cache invalidation by tenant\n  - Configurable TTL (5 minutes default)\n  - Metrics recording\n\n#### 4. REST API Endpoints\n\n- `/Users/tea/dev/VillageCompute/code/village-storefront/modules/core-platform/src/main/java/villagecompute/storefront/api/rest/ProductResource.java` - Public/Storefront endpoints:\n  - `GET /api/v1/catalog/products` - List/search with pagination, category/collection filtering\n  - `GET /api/v1/catalog/products/{id}` - Product details\n  - Feature flags: `catalog.search.enabled`, `catalog.variant-matrix.enabled`\n  - Response caching via `CatalogCacheService`\n\n- `CatalogAdminResource.java` - Admin endpoints (first 100 lines shown, continues with full CRUD):\n  - `GET /api/v1/admin/catalog/categories` - List categories with pagination\n  - `POST /api/v1/admin/catalog/categories` - Create category\n  - `GET/PUT/DELETE /api/v1/admin/catalog/categories/{id}`\n  - `GET /api/v1/admin/catalog/collections` - List collections\n  - `POST /api/v1/admin/catalog/collections` - Create collection\n  - `GET/PUT/DELETE /api/v1/admin/catalog/collections/{id}`\n  - Metrics recording via `CatalogMetrics`\n\n#### 5. Validation & Mappers\n\n- `CatalogValidator.java` - 150+ lines enforcing:\n  - Status transition rules (draft → active → archived → deleted with constraints)\n  - Slug uniqueness per tenant\n  - Product type validation (physical|digital|service)\n  - Collection type validation (manual|automatic)\n  - Required field checks\n\n- Mappers in `/services/mappers/`:\n  - `ProductMapper.java` - Entity ↔ DTO conversion\n  - `ProductVariantMapper.java` - Variant mapping\n  - `CategoryMapper.java` - Category DTO transformation\n  - `CollectionMapper.java` - Collection DTO transformation\n\n#### 6. Test Coverage\n\nComprehensive test suite with 9 dedicated catalog test files:\n\n1. **Unit/Integration Tests:**\n   - `CatalogServiceTest.java` - 150+ lines: CRUD operations, variant management, tenant isolation, search\n   - `CatalogValidatorTest.java` - Validation logic testing\n   - `CatalogMetricsTest.java` - Metrics recording verification\n   - `CatalogDtoMapperTest.java` - DTO transformation validation\n\n2. **REST API Tests:**\n   - `ProductResourceTest.java` - Storefront catalog API with tenant isolation, pagination, filtering\n   - `CatalogAdminResourceTest.java` - Admin API CRUD operations, tenant isolation\n   - `CatalogAdminImportExportIT.java` - End-to-end import/export integration tests\n\n3. **Job/Async Tests:**\n   - `CatalogImportJobHandlerTest.java` - CSV import processing\n   - `CatalogExportJobHandlerTest.java` - CSV export generation\n   - `CatalogJobServiceTest.java` - Job queue management\n\n4. **Infrastructure Tests:**\n   - `CollectionRepositoryTest.java` - Repository-level query testing\n\n#### 7. Job Framework\n\n- `CatalogImportJobHandler.java` - CSV import processor\n- `CatalogImportJobPayload.java` - Import job serialization\n- `CatalogExportJobHandler.java` - CSV export generator\n- `CatalogExportJobPayload.java` - Export job serialization\n- `CatalogJobScheduler.java` - Job scheduling automation\n\n#### 8. Supporting Infrastructure\n\n- **Metrics:** `CatalogMetrics.java` - Records product/collection create/update/delete operations\n- **Domain Events:** `DomainEventPublisher.java` integration for catalog events\n- **Caching:** `CatalogCacheService.java` with automatic cache invalidation\n- **Feature Toggles:** `FeatureToggle.java` integration for feature flags\n\n---\n\n### WHAT'S PRESENT BUT COULD NEED EXPANSION\n\n1. **Product-Category Relationships:**\n   - Many-to-many via `ProductCategory` join entity exists\n   - Queries like `findActiveByCategorySlug()` implemented\n   - Missing: Explicit repository for `ProductCategory` (only used via queries)\n\n2. **Product-Collection Relationships:**\n   - Many-to-many via `ProductCollection` join entity exists\n   - Queries like `findActiveByCollectionSlug()` implemented\n   - Missing: Explicit repository for `ProductCollection`\n\n3. **Variant Management:**\n   - Basic CRUD in `CatalogService` (create, list by product, find by SKU)\n   - Missing: Update variant, delete variant, variant inventory coordination\n\n4. **Category Hierarchy:**\n   - Parent-child relationships supported\n   - Missing: Breadcrumb generation, depth limiting, cyclic reference prevention\n\n5. **Collection Features:**\n   - Manual and automatic types supported\n   - `selectionRules` JSON field for automatic collections exists\n   - Missing: Automatic rule evaluation/execution logic\n\n6. **Product Images:**\n   - `ProductImage` entity exists for tracking metadata\n   - Missing: Repository, service methods, REST endpoints for image management\n\n---\n\n### WHAT'S MISSING (Based on Standard Ecommerce Features)\n\n1. **Variant Management Services:**\n   - No dedicated variant update/delete methods in `CatalogService`\n   - No variant inventory coordination\n   - Missing repository for direct variant queries beyond basic lookups\n\n2. **Category/Collection Management:**\n   - No explicit repositories for `ProductCategory`/`ProductCollection` join tables\n   - Missing service methods for adding/removing products from categories/collections\n   - Missing bulk operations (assign multiple products to category, etc.)\n\n3. **Advanced Catalog Features:**\n   - No product attributes system (color, size, material beyond variant JSON)\n   - No variant option management (defining available options globally)\n   - No bundle/kit support\n   - No product recommendations or related products\n\n4. **SEO & Publishing:**\n   - SEO metadata stored in JSON but no dedicated service\n   - No URL slug generation/management\n   - No meta tag generation\n   - No XML sitemap generation\n\n5. **Search & Discovery:**\n   - Basic text search on title/name/SKU\n   - Missing: Full-text search integration (Elasticsearch, database FTS)\n   - Missing: Faceted search (filter by attributes, price range, etc.)\n   - Missing: Search analytics\n\n6. **Performance Optimizations:**\n   - Cache strategy exists but limited scope\n   - Missing: Materialized views for category/collection counts\n   - Missing: Product listing materialization\n   - Missing: Search result pre-computation\n\n7. **Admin Features Missing:**\n   - No bulk product import/update beyond async job framework\n   - No product duplication/cloning\n   - No variant generation from options\n   - No inventory forecasting\n\n8. **Variant-Specific Gaps:**\n   - No dedicated variant REST endpoints (`/api/v1/admin/variants`)\n   - No variant barcode management UI\n   - No variant selection logic for storefront (size charts, etc.)\n\n---\n\n### QUALITY & STANDARDS COMPLIANCE\n\n**Strengths:**\n- All code follows Quarkus best practices (PanacheRepositoryBase, ApplicationScoped)\n- Comprehensive tenant isolation at every layer\n- Structured logging with OpenTelemetry integration\n- Full test coverage with integration and E2E tests\n- Validation framework integrated throughout\n- Feature flag support for gradual rollout\n- Metrics instrumentation for observability\n- Proper error handling with custom exceptions\n\n**Code Stats:**\n- Services: 705 lines (CatalogService), 224 lines (CatalogJobService)\n- Repositories: 268 lines (ProductRepository), 158 lines (CollectionRepository)\n- Tests: 9 dedicated test files covering unit, integration, and E2E scenarios\n- Models: 5 core entities + 3 association/support entities\n\n---\n\n### RECOMMENDATIONS\n\n**For Short Term:**\n1. Add explicit repositories for `ProductCategory` and `ProductCollection` join tables\n2. Implement variant CRUD operations (update, delete with inventory cleanup)\n3. Add bulk product-category/collection assignment endpoints\n\n**For Medium Term:**\n1. Implement automatic collection rule evaluation\n2. Add full-text search with Elasticsearch or PostgreSQL FTS\n3. Create variant option management system\n4. Add product duplication/cloning features\n\n**For Long Term:**\n1. Product recommendation engine\n2. Advanced search with faceting and analytics\n3. SEO optimization tools (auto slug generation, meta tag templates)\n4. Bundle/kit product support"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: abda588 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)"}]
